    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0536" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857 Ar 1/89½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">21 August, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have your letter about
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi>, and find myself in substantial
                    agreement with it.</p>
                <p>I do not think that an immediate summons of the Cabinet would be wise. We should
                    first know all the facts. So soon as they are known we ought of course to find
                    the views of our colleagues. Haste in the matter would be likely to give the
                    country the wrong impression, I fear with regard to our frame of mind.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
